  "summary": {
    "plain": "After over two years with 18 crystals, AMoRE-I saw no indication of neutrinoless double beta decay of molybdenum-100 and set a lower limit of 2.9 x 10^24 years on its half-life at 90% confidence.",
    "technical": "Exposure 8.02 kg yr (3.89 kg yr of 100Mo), background 0.025 +/- 0.002 counts/keV/kg/yr near the Q-value; effective Majorana mass limit m_bb < (210-610) meV with several nuclear matrix-element models (Phys. Rev. Lett. 134, 082501 (2025))."
  },
